         recommended test: A run configured with the batch setting enabled submits its Claude model calls through the Message Batches API rather than the direct Messages API.
           inputs:  Call measure_instability with batch=True and no client_factory, using a benchmark case, a perturbation (so the perturbed draw and comparison path run), and a comparison_client left as None, with a fake Anthropic SDK provider (FakeProvider fixture) so nothing reaches the network. Also build a client via ModelClient(...) directly with a batcher to show the contrast.
           detects: The batcher reaches a client only through `RunConfig.build_client`, and it is passed to `ModelClient` only when `self.batch` is true. Any client built another way, such as a `client_factory` or a direct `ModelClient(...)` construction in other entry points, gets no batcher. Within `measure_instability`, `comparison_client` is also never given one. Those Claude calls then go direct despite the run's batch setting.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion batch-api-opt-in

