         recommended test: A run's configuration object exposes the batch-API setting, and the code that decides how model calls are sent reads the setting from that configuration rather than from a separate global or per-call source.
           inputs:  A RunConfig(batch=True, mode=RECORD, transcript_root=tmp_path); call build_client() once (creating the batcher lazily), then take copy = config.model_copy(update={'transcript_root': other}) and build clients from both; also the reverse order (copy before any client is built, then build from each).
           detects: The batcher is held as a pydantic private attribute created lazily on the RunConfig. model_copy copies private state shallowly. If a config is copied after its batcher was created, the copy shares the same batcher, so two runs that should each hold their own state share one. If it is copied before, each copy gets a separate batcher, which breaks one-batcher-per-run sharing.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion batch-setting-in-run-configuration

