    [other] recording-notes-batch-origin/note-reflects-intent-not-actual-transport
      The note is set from the precomputed `batched` flag, not from evidence that the request went through the batch transport. If LiteLLM ignores the injected client, or the request fails over to a direct send, the recording would claim a batch send that did not happen. Equally, a call that was batched could go unmarked.
