  byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes
    [unenforced_on_one_path] byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes/sent-via-field-differs-recording
      A batched call's transcript record gains a `sent_via: "batch"` field that a direct call's record lacks. If transcripts are part of the serialized review state, a batched run and a direct run over the same input no longer compare byte-for-byte equal.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#8
      src/acceptance/llm_batch.py#0
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 259 skipped once the defect was covered
    [unenforced_on_one_path] byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes/batched-cost-halved-in-record
      The recorded `usage.cost_usd` is multiplied by 0.5 only on the batch path. The same request therefore records a different cost depending on send mode. Float scaling can also shift the serialized digits.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#8
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 259 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes/batch-usage-and-cache-fields-differ
      The batched reply is re-serialized into a synthetic httpx.Response and then parsed. Usage fields such as cache read and creation tokens come from the batch results, which can differ from a direct call because batch cache hits are best-effort. Recorded usage can therefore differ between modes for identical requests.
      src/acceptance/llm_batch.py#0
      src/acceptance/llm.py#8
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 259 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes/observed-call-order-depends-on-concurrency
      Batched clients run stages at up to 512 calls in flight instead of 8, and batch answers arrive in arbitrary order. Anything appended in completion order, such as `_observed_calls` or logs written inside a call, can then be ordered differently from a direct run. That makes the serialized state differ between send modes or send mixes.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#5
      src/acceptance/concurrency.py#1
      src/acceptance/defects/enumeration.py#0
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#0
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 251 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] byte-identical-review-state-across-send-modes/batch-flag-leaks-into-serialized-config
      `RunConfig.batch` is a new public field on a pydantic model. If the config, or anything derived from it, is dumped into review state or provenance, the flag makes two runs over the same input serialize differently depending on send mode.
      src/acceptance/config.py#2
      src/acceptance/benchmark/instability.py#0
