  [already_present] batch-setting-in-run-configuration/batcher-shared-across-config-copies
    candidate edits: 1 asked for, 0 set aside, none used
    pairs: 0 settled by the run, 263 put to the model, 0 dropped as not worth asking, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    _batcher is a pydantic PrivateAttr created lazily in _run_batcher (lines 218-221). Pydantic's model_copy goes through __copy__, which shallow-copies private state, so a copy made after the batcher exists shares it with the original. A copy made before first use gets its own batcher. Which of the two happens depends on timing, which is the DEFECTIVE behaviour. The repair overrides __copy__ so every copy starts with no batcher and builds its own on first use.

